The '''Quell system''' was located in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] and contained the [[planet]] [[Quell]]. Throughout the [[Clone Wars]], the [[star system]] was heavily contested by both of the war's sides' respective forces, including the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[Providence-class Dreadnought|''Providence''-class Dreadnought]] ''[[Lucid Voice]]''.

In [[21 BBY]], during the war, Quell served as the site of an [[Battle of Quell|engagement]] between a [[Galactic Republic]] task force led by [[Jedi General]] [[Aayla Secura]] and a Confederacy [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|naval]] [[TF-1726's squadron|squadron]] [[Commanding officer|commanded]] by [[T-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid|T-series tactical droid]] [[TF-1726]]. During the battle, the Confederacy was able to inflict heavy casualties upon the Republic's forces, while also claiming victory in the end.

==Description==
The Quell system was located in the distant reaches of [[the galaxy]],<ref name="Battles">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref> in the regions known as the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> and the [[New Territories]].<ref name="New Territories" /> The [[Nuiri sector]] [[Star system|system]] was situated in grid square Q-6 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="Appendix" /> the [[star]] system contained the [[planet]] [[Quell]], which was located in its far reaches.<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> It was also located along the [[Salin Corridor]] [[hyperspace route]],<ref name="Salin" /> which connected the system to the astronomical object [[Yalbec Prime]] and<ref name="Timelines">{{GalaxyMapPoster}}</ref> the planet<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Lola Sayu]].<ref name="Timelines" />

==History==
{{Quote|Hurry, Skywalker. We're depending on you.|Aayla Secura, as her forces begin to suffer heavy casualties|<ref name="Jedi Crash" />}}
[[File:Liberty_bridge.png|thumb|left|270px|A squadron of Separatist ''Munificent''-class star frigates advances on Aayla Secura's flagship during the Battle of Quell.]]
Throughout the [[Clone Wars]] fought between the [[Galactic Republic]] and [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], the Quell system was heavily contested by both of the warring factions' forces, which included the Confederacy's [[Providence-class Dreadnought|''Providence''-class Dreadnought]] ''[[Lucid Voice]]''.<ref name="Tarkin" /> During the war,<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> in [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TCWcanondates|113}}</ref> the upper [[atmosphere]] of Quell served as the site of a [[Battle of Quell|battle]], where a Republic [[Aayla Secura's task force|task force]] of [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyers]] led by [[Jedi General]] [[Aayla Secura]] was assaulted by a Confederacy [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|naval]] [[TF-1726's squadron|squadron]]<ref name="Battles" /> of [[Munificent-class star frigate|''Munificent''-class star frigates]] [[Commanding officer|commanded]] by the [[T-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid]] [[TF-1726]].<ref name="Jedi Crash" />

During the battle, which led to heavy Republic casualties that included the loss of all three of Secura's [[Star Destroyer]]s, the [[Jedi Master]] managed to escape the destruction of her [[flagship]], the [[Liberty (Venator-class)|''Liberty'']], as well as the battle with the help of fellow [[Jedi]] [[General]] [[Anakin Skywalker]]; his [[Padawan]], [[Ahsoka Tano]]; and [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex|CT-7567]]. Arriving in the Quell system aboard their Venator, the ''[[Resolute]]'', in order to aid in Secura's engagement with the Separatist [[squadron]], Skywalker used a [[Unidentified Consular-class cruiser (Quell)|rescue frigate]] to dock with Secura's [[starship]] and retrieve her before its destruction. However, during the Jedi escape from the Star Destroyer, the [[frigate]] suffered damage, which resulted in the activation of its [[hyperdrive]] and subsequent jump through [[hyperspace]] to the planet [[Maridun]].<ref name="Jedi Crash" />

[[File:Resolute_hyperspace.png|thumb|right|270px|Anakin Skywalker's ''Venator''-class Star Destroyer, the ''Resolute'', races to help Aayla Secura in the Quell system.]]
The Battle of Quell was an unqualified victory for the Confederacy, and it revealed that the Republic initially struggled to maintain control in the Outer Rim, a region where acts of separatism had flourished by that [[time]]. Furthermore, the battle proved that the Republic's ultimate triumph in the war would not be easily won.<ref name="Battles" /> Sometime after her defeat at Quell,<ref name="Quell card">{{Destiny|set=Way of the Force|cardname=Quell|link=http://swdestinydb.com/card/07150}}</ref> between [[20 BBY]] and [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Quell card date note">{{Destiny|set=Way of the Force|cardname=Quell|link=http://swdestinydb.com/card/07150}} shows the [[327th Star Corps]] with [[Phase II clone trooper armor]], which makes its first chorological appearance in "[[Water War]]," while {{Film|III}} establishes that [[armor]] was used for the rest of the [[Clone Wars]]. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]'' dates the events of "Water War" to [[20 BBY]] and those of ''Revenge of the Sith'' to [[19 BBY]], the events pictured on the Quell card must occur between those two [[Standard year|years]].</ref> Secura and her clone troopers from the [[327th Star Corps]] returned to the planet's surface, where they engaged in combat with an adversary.<ref name="Quell card" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Quell system first appeared in "[[Jedi Crash]],"<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> the thirteenth episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]] of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television series, which aired on [[January 16]], [[2009]].<ref name="Jedi Crash Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode013.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Jedi Crash}}</ref> The system was identified in the episode's opening newsreel.<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> The episode's script described the Battle of Quell as taking place within [[Realspace|space]] around Quell, but the engagement was instead moved to the planet's upper atmosphere for dramatic effect as the show entered pre-production.<ref name="Trivia Gallery">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/jedi-crash-trivia-gallery|text="Jedi Crash" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 2}}</ref>

